ican incumbent Nick Begich III seeks a second full term in Alaska's at-large House seat against little-known Democrat Eric Hafner, with independent Bill Hill and a Libertarian also on the ballot. Begich has raised $5.5 million and holds $3.1 million on hand, dwarfing his rivals' finances. Nine expert ratings cluster at Likely R, with the Silver Bulletin going further to Solid R, and Polymarket prices the Democrat's chances near 5%. No usable general-election head-to-head polls exist; the few available surveys are mostly hypothetical and dated, though they consistently show Republican strength. The state's R+6 lean and Begich's incumbency advantage point to a comfortable but not overwhelming Republican win, with ranked-choice tabulation and Hill's independent bid the main sources of uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1234, "margin": -7.11}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1042, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0943, "margin": -9.0}]}